facts:
On a $10 \times 10$ grid ($100$ squares), each shaded square is $1\%$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.5]
\fill[gray!40] (0,9) rectangle (1,10);
\draw[step=1] (0,0) grid (10,10);
\node[below] at (5,-0.6) {one shaded square $=1\%$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
The grid represents one whole divided into $100$ equal squares.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.35]
\fill[gray!40] (0,0) rectangle (4,10);
\fill[gray!40] (4,0) rectangle (5,3);
\draw[step=1] (0,0) grid (10,10);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) What percentage is shaded?
(b) What percentage is not shaded?

